      "13.1.3.3 Electrical Conductivity None of the period 3 oxides have any free or mobile electrons. It means that none of them will conduct electricity when they are in solid state. The ionic oxides can, however, conduct electricity in molten state because of the movement of ions towards the opposite electrodes.",
      "13.1.4 Acid-Base Behaviour of the Oxides",
