      "13.1.6.1 Sodium and Magnesium Hydroxides Sodium hydroxide (NaOH) is a white solids having soapy touch. Skin contact with concentrated caustic soda can cause serious chemical burns. This is highly hygroscopic. Sodium hydroxide is only slightly soluble in alcohols. It is one of the most soluble substances in water evolving a considerable amount of heat.",
