      "Effect of Heat on Nitrates, Carbonates and Hydrogen-Carbonates explaining the Trend in Terms of the Polarizing Ability of the",
      "Positive Ion",
      "Compounds of Group - IA elements are more stable to heat than the corresponding compounds of Group - IIA elements with the exception of lithium compounds.",
      "Effect of Heat on Nitrates",
      "-",
      "In Group – IA the lithium nitrates decomposes on the same way as the nitrates of Group-IIA. Group - IIA nitrates tend to decompose on heating to produce metal oxide, nitrogen dioxide (brown fumes) and",
      "oxygen.",
      "Tidbit",
      "The ability of a cation to distort",
      "an anion is known as its polarization power and the tendency of the anion to become polarized by the cation is known as its polarizability.",
      "Lithium nitrate on decomposition produces lithium oxide, nitrogen dioxide and oxygen.",
      "4LINO 300",
