      "The word 'Aufbau' is derived from the German language and can be translated as construct or build up.",
      "Aufbau principle states that electrons are",
      "Generally, the electronic configuration of transition elements is (n-1) d1-\"ns' Scandium (Z=21), the first transition metal in this series, has the configuration [Ar]3d',4s2. Addition of electron to the 3d sub-shell continues until, at zinc (Z=30), the 3d sub-shell is filled, with the 4s sub-shell still containing two electrons. However, there are two regularities, one at chromium (Z=24) and the other at copper (Z=29). The electronic configuration of chromium (Z = 24) is [Ar]3d3, 4s and not [Ar]3d,452 as we might expect. A similar break in the pattern is observed for copper, whose electronic configuration is [Ar] 3d10,4s', rather than [Ar] 3d,4s2.",
