        "theory": "Benzene is aromatic hydrocarbon. Its molecular formula is C6H6.\nThe representation of a real structure as a weighted average of two or more contributing structures is called resonance.\nThe contributing structures are called canonical forms and real structure is called resonance hybrid.\nElectrophilic aromatic substitution reactions are those in which hydrogen of benzene is replaced by an electrophile.\nCarbocation contains a positive charge on carbon atom.\nThe substituents which direct the second substituent to ortho and para position simultaneously are called ortho/para directing.\nThe substituents which direct the second incoming substituent to meta position are called meta-directing.\n157\n*\nNOT FOR SALE\nExercise\nQ I. Choose the correct one from the given options.\n1. The number of possible isomers for an alkane having the molecular formula CsH12 is\na. 2\nb. 3\nc. 4\n2. 2,2,3,3-terabromobutane when heated with zinc dust, yields\na. but-1-yne\nc. isobutylene\nb. but-2-yne\nd. pent-1-yne\n3. But-2-yne can be converted into cis-but-2-ene by using\na. H2/Ni\nc. Na/liq. NH,\nb. Lindlar&#x27;s catalyst\nd. Zn/HCl\nWhen excess of HCI is added to acetylene, the product is\na. vinyl chloride.\nc. 1,2-dichloroethane.\nb. ethyl chloride.\nd. 1,1-dichloroethane.\n5. The homolytic fission of C-H bond in an alkane results in\na. carbanion.\nc. alkyl free radical.\nb. carbocation.\n6. The groups that deactivate benzene ring and is o/p-directing\nb. -OH\nd. 5\nd. all of these.\nd. Cl\nc. - OCH1\na. -NH2 7. Alkene that can be expected to exhibit geometrical isomerism\na. but-1-ene\nc. 2-methylpropene\n8. How many isomers are possible for C2H2O?\na. 2\nb. 4\n9. Addition of HBr to isobutylene mainly gives\na. n-butyl bromide.\nc. sec-butyl bromide.\nb. 2-methylbut-2-ene\nd. none of these\nc. 8\nb. isobutyl bromide.\nwaz e in\nd. tert-butyl bromide.\nd. 5\nQ\n10. An alkene upon ozonolysis yield a mixture of acetone and acetaldehyde. The\nalkene is\na. isobutylene\nc. 2-methylbut-2-ene\nb. but-2-ene\nd. pent-2-ene\n11. Dehydrohalogenation of alkylhalide is carried out in presence of\na. Zn dust.\nc. alcoholic KOH.\nb. conc. H2SO4-\n158\nd. aqueous KOH.\n12. Which of the following molecules contain chiral center?\na. n-butyl bromide\nc. sec-butyl bromide\n13. In the following reaction C,H,CH,+ Cl2\nwhat type of reaction has taken?\na. Electrophilic substitution\nc. Free radical substitution\nNOT FOR SALE\nb. isobutyl bromide d. tert-butyl bromide\nUV. light",
        "content": "Benzene is aromatic hydrocarbon. Its molecular formula is C6H6.<br>The representation of a real structure as a weighted average of two or more contributing structures is called resonance.<br>The contributing structures are called canonical forms and real structure is called resonance hybrid.<br>Electrophilic aromatic substitution reactions are those in which hydrogen of benzene is replaced by an electrophile.<br>Carbocation contains a positive charge on carbon atom.<br>The substituents which direct the second substituent to ortho and para position simultaneously are called ortho/para directing.<br>The substituents which direct the second incoming substituent to meta position are called meta-directing.<br>157<br>*<br>NOT FOR SALE<br>Exercise<br>Q I. Choose the correct one from the given options.<br>1. The number of possible isomers for an alkane having the molecular formula CsH12 is<br>a. 2<br>b. 3<br>c. 4<br>2. 2,2,3,3-terabromobutane when heated with zinc dust, yields<br>a. but-1-yne<br>c. isobutylene<br>b. but-2-yne<br>d. pent-1-yne<br>3. But-2-yne can be converted into cis-but-2-ene by using<br>a. H2/Ni<br>c. Na/liq. NH,<br>b. Lindlar&#x27;s catalyst<br>d. Zn/HCl<br>When excess of HCI is added to acetylene, the product is<br>a. vinyl chloride.<br>c. 1,2-dichloroethane.<br>b. ethyl chloride.<br>d. 1,1-dichloroethane.<br>5. The homolytic fission of C-H bond in an alkane results in<br>a. carbanion.<br>c. alkyl free radical.<br>b. carbocation.<br>6. The groups that deactivate benzene ring and is o/p-directing<br>b. -OH<br>d. 5<br>d. all of these.<br>d. Cl<br>c. - OCH1<br>a. -NH2 7. Alkene that can be expected to exhibit geometrical isomerism<br>a. but-1-ene<br>c. 2-methylpropene<br>8. How many isomers are possible for C2H2O?<br>a. 2<br>b. 4<br>9. Addition of HBr to isobutylene mainly gives<br>a. n-butyl bromide.<br>c. sec-butyl bromide.<br>b. 2-methylbut-2-ene<br>d. none of these<br>c. 8<br>b. isobutyl bromide.<br>waz e in<br>d. tert-butyl bromide.<br>d. 5<br>Q<br>10. An alkene upon ozonolysis yield a mixture of acetone and acetaldehyde. The<br>alkene is<br>a. isobutylene<br>c. 2-methylbut-2-ene<br>b. but-2-ene<br>d. pent-2-ene<br>11. Dehydrohalogenation of alkylhalide is carried out in presence of<br>a. Zn dust.<br>c. alcoholic KOH.<br>b. conc. H2SO4-<br>158<br>d. aqueous KOH.<br>12. Which of the following molecules contain chiral center?<br>a. n-butyl bromide<br>c. sec-butyl bromide<br>13. In the following reaction C,H,CH,+ Cl2<br>what type of reaction has taken?<br>a. Electrophilic substitution<br>c. Free radical substitution<br>NOT FOR SALE<br>b. isobutyl bromide d. tert-butyl bromide<br>UV. light",
        "rules": [],
        "sciNote": "Benzene is aromatic hydrocarbon. Its molecular formula is C6H6.\nThe representation of a real structure as a weighted average of two or more contributing structures is called resonance.\nThe contributing structures are called canonical forms and real structure is called resonance hybrid.\nElectrophilic aromatic substitution reactions are those in which hydrogen of benzene is replaced by an electrophile.\nCarbocation contains a positive charge on carbon atom.\nThe substituents which direct the second substituent to ortho and para position simultaneously are called ortho/para directing.\nThe substituents which direct the second incoming substituent to meta position are called meta-directing.\n157\n*\nNOT FOR SALE\nExercise\nQ I. Choose the correct one from the given options.\n1. The number of possible isomers for an alkane having the molecular formula CsH12 is\na. 2\nb. 3\nc. 4\n2. 2,2,3,3-terabromobutane when heated with zinc dust, yields\na. but-1-yne\nc. isobutylene\nb. but-2-yne\nd. pent-1-yne\n3. But-2-yne can be converted into cis-but-2-ene by using\na. H2/Ni\nc. Na/liq. NH,\nb. Lindlar's catalyst\nd. Zn/HCl\nWhen excess of HCI is added to acetylene, the product is\na. vinyl chloride.\nc. 1,2-dichloroethane.\nb. ethyl chloride.\nd. 1,1-dichloroethane.\n5. The homolytic fission of C-H bond in an alkane results in\na. carbanion.\nc. alkyl free radical.\nb. carbocation.\n6. The groups that deactivate benzene ring and is o/p-directing\nb. -OH\nd. 5\nd. all of these.\nd. Cl\nc. - OCH1\na. -NH2 7. Alkene that can be e",
