      "16.2.3 Structure",
      "16.2.3.1 Structure of Ethane",
      "In ethane (C2H,) each carbon atom is bonded to four other atoms, so it uses. sp3-hybrid orbitals to form these bonds. There are six C-H covalent bonds and one C-C covalent bond. Each of the C-H bonds, is the result of linear overlap of sp3-hybrid orbital of carbon and Is orbital of hydrogen. The C-C sigma bond is formed due to the overlap of sp3-hybrid orbitals, one from each carbon atom (Fig. 16.1). All the C-H and C-C bonds are sigma (5) bonds. All the bond angles are 109.5° (tetrahedral geometry). The C-C bond length is 154 pm and each C-H bond length is 109.5 pm.",
