      "Thus, a mixture of all the four substitution products i.e. methyl chloride, methylene chloride, chloroform and carbon tetrachloride are obtained. The extent of their concentration in the mixture depends on the relative amounts of chlorine and methane. If chlorine is taken in excess, the reaction goes to the final substitution product and carbon tetrachloride is the major product. On the contrary, when chlorine is limited and methane is in excess, the major product of the reaction is",
      "methyl chloride.",
