      "Tidbit",
      "In 1993, the IUPAC recommended a logical change in the positions of the numbers used in names. Instead of placing the numbers before the root name (1-butene),",
      "Consider ethene (CH) to illustrate the structure of alkenes. In ethene, each carbon atom has three sp2-hybridized orbitals which are coplanar. One of the sp2-hybrid orbitals of one carbon atom overlaps linearly with that of another carbon atom to form a sigma (8) bond. The other two sp- hybrid orbitals of each carbon atom overlap with Is orbital of hydrogen atoms to form C-H sigma bonds. The unhybridized p-orbitals of the two perpendicular to the plane of hybridized orbitals, overlap in a side-wise (parallel) fashion to form a pi (x) bond between the two carbon atoms. (Figure.16.3).",
