      "sodium alkynide",
      "Acetylene and other terminal alkynes are more acidic than alkanes and alkenes, as clear from pKa values given in Table 16.5. The acidity of an acetylenic hydrogen is due to sp-hybridization of triple bonded carbon atom. A sp-hybrid orbital has 50% s character in it and renders the carbon atom more electronegative than sp2 and sp'-hybridized carbons. As a result, the sp-hybridized carbon atoms of a terminal alkyne pulls the electrons more strongly making the attached hydrogen atom slightly acidic.",
