      "acetyl cation (Electrophile)",
      "An electrophilic substitution reaction of benzene results only in the formation of one monosubstituted product because all hydrogen atoms of benzene ring are equivalent. However, second substituent can occupy any of the three remaining position to form three isomeric (ortho, meta and para) disubstituted products. It is expected that ortho, para disubstituted products should be formed with ratio of 2:2:1, as given",
