      "16.8.5.2 Making Polysubstituted Benzenes",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "Polysubstituted benzenes are the derivatives of benzene in which two or more hydrogen atoms have been substituted by other atoms or group of atoms. We have to keep in mind the activating and directing effect of first substituents on the ring while planning the synthesis of a polysubstituted benzene derivative.",
      "For example, the synthesis of bromonitrobenzene from benzene require the introduction of -NO2 and -Br groups in two consecutive electrophilic substitution reactions i.e. nitration and bromination. Either of the two substituents can be introduced into the benzene ring first and then the other. If benzene is first brominated and then nitrated, we will get mainly a mixture of o- and p-bromonitrobenzene because bromo group is ortho/para orienting.",
      "Br",
