        "id": "17.15",
        "title": "17.3.7.5 Preparation of Diazonium Salts",
        "theory": "In sickle cell anemia, the abnormal hemoglobin (Hemoglobin-S) sticks together when it gives up its oxygen to the tissues. These clumps cause red blood cells to become stiff and &#x27;shaped like a sickle.\nChlorophyll helps do the job of hemoglobin when ingested. Promote the health of circulation, cleanse the body, increase the number of red blood cells and therefore increase oxygen throughout the body, in other words, Chlorophyll helps build hemoglobin. This is exactly what our sickle cell babies and others need, to build hemoglobin.\n188\nKey Points\nGeneral formula of alkyl halide is R-X.\nNOT FOR SALE\nThe molecule which undergoes substitution reaction is called &#x27;substrate&#x27;. The group or species which leaves the substrate is called &quot;leaving group&quot;. SN1 mechanism is defined as that nucleophilic substitution reaction in which only one molecule is involved in rate determing or slow step.\nThose nucleophilic substitution reactions in which two species are involved in the rate determing or slow step are called SN2 reactions.\nThe primary alkyl halides undergo SN2 mechanism while tertiary alkyl halides undergo Sul mechanism.\nIn polar solvent secondary alkyl halides follow SN1-mechanism while in non- polar solvents follow SN2-mechanism.\nDuring elimination reaction two strong sigma bonds are broken and a new weaker pi bond is formed.\nEl stands for unimolecular elimination while E2 stands for bimolecular elimination reaction.\nThose organic compounds which contain at least one carbon-metal bond in their structure are known as organometallic compounds.\nAmines are derivatives of NH, in which one or more hydrogen atom have been replaced by one or more similar or different alkyl group.\nDue to presence of lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atoms (R-NH,) amines. are basic in nature.\nCC\nCCCC\nC\n189\nNOT FOR SALE\nExercise\nQI. Choose the correct one from the given options.\n1. The reaction of CH Mgl with acetone followed by hydrolysis gives\na. tert-butyl alcohol.\nc. n-butyl alcohol.\nb. sec-butyl alcohol.\nd. none of these.\n2. Which one of the following halide is most reactive towards nucleophilic\nsubstitution reaction?\na. CH,Br\nb. CH,l\nc. C2H,F\nd. C2H,C\n3. An electron deficient specie is\na. electrophile\nb. nucleophile\nc. Lewis base\nd. none\n4. R-CH-X is an example of\na. primary alkyl halide.\nc. tertiary alkyl halide.\nb. secondary alkyl halide.\nd. both (a) and (b).\n5. The carbon atom carrying positive charge and attached to three other atoms or\ngroups is called\na. Carbocation.\nc. Oxonium ion\nb. Carbanion\n6. Grignard reagent can be represented by general formula\na. R-Mg-NH2\nc. R-Mg-OH\nd. Carbene\nb. R-Mg-OR\nd. R-Mg-X\netate\n7. The end product of reaction of a Grignard reagent with ethyl acetate is\na. primary alcohol.\nc. tertiary alcohol.\n8. An electron-pair donor is\na. Lewis acid\nb. Nucleophile\nb. secondary alcohol. d. methyl alcohol.\naw\nb. Electrophile\nd. Free radical\nin\n9. In secondary alkyl halides the carbon atom to which the halo group is attached is\nin turn bonded directly to\na. one other carbon.\nc. three other carbons.\n10. Characteristics of SNl reaction is\na. 100% inversion\nc. partial racemization\nb. two other carbons.\nd. four other carbons.\nb. 100% retention d. none of these\n190\n11. Which of the following solvent is aprotic?\na. Acetone\nc. Water",
