      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "alogen derivatives of alkanes are called haloalkanes. Haloalkanes are formed by placing one or more hydrogen atoms from alkanes by halogens. They are also called ganohalogen compounds. Haloalkanes may be monohaloalkanes, dihaloalkanes, haloalkanes etc., depending upon the number of halogen atoms present in the",
      "olecule.",
      "lonohaloalkanes are usually called alkyl halides. The functional group of alkyl halides halogen. They are represented by R-X, where R- is an alkyl group represented by Hand-X is halogen which is the functional group. The general formula of alkyl lides is CHX, where n represents the number of carbon atoms.",
      "Ilkyl halides are classified according to the nature of the carbon atom bonded to e halogen. If the halogen-bearing carbon is bonded to one carbon atom, it is imary (1°) and the alkyl halide is a primary alkyl halide. If two carbon atoms are nded to the halogen-bearing carbon, it is secondary (2°) and the compound is a condary alkyl halide. A tertiary alkyl halide (3°) has three other carbon atoms. nded to the halogen-bearing carbon atom. If the halogen-bearing carbon atom is methyl group (bonded to no other carbon atoms), the compound is a methyl",
