      "The intermediate carbocation is planar, the nucleophile attack from either side. If a nucleophile attacks the carbocation from the side of the leaving group, the product molecule shows retention of configuration. Attack from the side opposite to leaving group, gives a product molecule showing inversion of configuration. If the reactant is chiral, mixture of two enantiomers (Section 16.6.5) are produced, called racemic mixture and this process is called racemization. Racemization is simply a combination of retention and inversion. However in SN1, the product is rarely completely racemic",
