      "17.1.7.1 Overview",
      "We have already discussed that alkyl halides undergo substitution as well as elimination reactions in (Section 17.1.5). When treated with a strong base, an alkyl halide can undergo a type of elimination process, called 1,2-elimination, also known as B-elimination, in which a proton is removed from the ẞ position, the halide is ejected as a leaving group from the a position and a double bond is formed between. the a and ẞ positions:",
