      "O(C2H1)1",
      "O(C2H1)2",
      "Figure 17.4 Tetrahedral dietherate of Grignard reagent.",
      "17.2.2 Reactivity of Grignard Reagents",
      "The carbon magnesium bond of Grignard reagent is polar in nature. This is due to higher electronegativity of carbon than magnesium. So the electronic density is lying close to carbon than magnesium. As a result of this electronegativity difference, the carbon atom has a partial negative while magnesium has a partial positive charge.",
      "R-MgX",
      "The alkyl group being an electron rich centre, acts as carbanion or nucleophile. It would attack polarized molecules at the point of low electronic density. Therefore, the characteristic reactions of Grignard reagents are nucleophilic substitution and nucleophilic addition reactions.",
      "17.2.3 Reactions of Grignard Reagents",
      "Grignard reagents are highly reactive compounds. Therefore, they react with many rganic and inorganic compounds to produce a large number of valuable products.",
      "ome of these reactions are as follows.",
