      "methyl alcohol",
      "Figure 18.2 Comparison of structure of phenol and methyl alcohol",
      "In phenol the six carbon atoms are sp-hybridized forming a hexagonal ring with internal angles of 120°. In the bonds C-O and O-H, bond lengths are 136 pm and 96 pm respectively. Since the bonds formed by sp-hybridized carbon, are shorter than those formed by sp'-hybridized carbon, therefore the C-O bond length is slightly less than the C-O bond length in methanol (142 pm). In resonance terms, the shorter carbon-oxygen bond distance in phenol is attributed to the partial",
