        "sciNote": "The reaction is catalyzed by an acid. The mechanism is similar to general acid-catalysed\nmechanism discussed in Section 19.6.1.\n0:\nडिप\nIdehyde/ketone oxonium ion\nOH\nOH,\nNH2X\n-C-\n+ H2O\n-H+\n-H+\nXN-H\ncondensation\naddition product\nNHX\neactions of ammonia and ammonia derivatives are given below.\nproduct\n¥\n239\n*\nH\n401\n0\nH\nC- aldehyde/ketone\n+ H-N-H\nC\n+ H2O\nimine\nammonia\nR\nN\nH\nC- + H-N-R\nC- + H2O\nN-substituted imine\naldehyde/ketone\n1o-amine\n(sec-imine)\nOH\nN\nH\nH+\naldehyde/ketone\nC- +H-N-OH\nhydroxylamine\nC-\noxime\n+ H2O\nNH2\nH\nCH2O\n+ H−NNH,\naldehyde/ketone\nhydrazine\n0\nH\nhydrazone\nNH−CH,\nH*\n-C+H2O\nphenyl hydrazine\nphenyl hydrazone\nC- + H−N-NH—CH,\naldehyde/ketone\n19.6.3.5 Using Oxygen Nucleophiles\nWater and alcohols are oxygen nucleophiles. They can add to carbonyl group to for\naddition products.\na. Using Water\naw\nWhen aldehydes or ketones react with water, they add a water molecule and for geminal diols (1,1-diols). The reaction is called hydration and can be catalyzed by acid\nor any hydroxide base.\nOH\n-c-\nHor OH\n+ H-OH\n-C-\naldehyde/ketone\nwater",
