      "CHO",
      "benzene-1,4-dicarbaldehyde",
      "Aldehydes and ketones have the same general formula, CnH2O and can exhibit functional group isomerism e.g. propanal and propanone are functional groups isomers. Aldehydes and ketones also show tautomerism (Section 16.6.1).",
      "229",
      "19.2",
      "Structure",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "Let us consider formaldehyde as an example to illustrate the structure of carbonyl group of aldehyde and ketone. The carbon and oxygen in the carbonyl group, present in aldehydes and ketones are linked by a sigma bond and a pi bond. Both carbon as well as oxygen of the carbonyl group are sp2-hybridized. The carbon-oxygen sigma and pi bonds are formed by linear sp2-sp2 and sidewise overlap of p orbitals respectively. Two of the sp2-hybrid orbitals of oxygen has two unshared electron pairs, while two of the sp2-hybrid orbitals of carbon overlap with s orbitals of two hydrogen atoms to form carbon-hydrogen sigma bonds in formaldehyde (Figure 19.1).",
