        "theory": "b. alcoholysis\nd. hydrolysis\n269\nQ2. Write short answers of the following questions.\n1. Why anhydrous acetic acid is known as glacial acetic acid?\n11.\nvi.\nvil.\nNOT FOR SALE\nThe boiling points of carboxylic acids are higher than corresponding alcohols. Explain\nbriefly.\nHow carboxylic acids are stronger acids than phenol, alcohols and water?\nWhy methanoic acid is stronger acid than ethanoic acid?\nChloroacetic acid is a derivative of acetic acid. Why chloroacetic acid is stronger acid\nthan acetic acid?\nHow carboxylic acids can be obtained readily by the oxidation of primary alcohols? Carboxylic acids are less reactive towards nucleophile, compared to aldehydes. Why? viii. Why amides are the least reactive derivatives of carboxylic acid, towards nucleophile? Esters can be hydrolysed in both acidic and basic conditions. Why base hydrolysis of esters is also called saponification?\nix.\nX.\nAcid halides are the most reactive of all acid derivatives towards nucleophiles. Explain briefly.\nQ3. Write detail answers of the following questions.\n1.\nExplain the acidity of carboxylic acids. How their acid strength is affected by\nelectron donating and withdrawing substitutions?\nHow will you prepare acetic acid by using?\niii. an alcohol\n2.\ni. a nitrile\nii. a Grignard reagent\niv. an aldehyde\n3.\ni. acetyl chloride\nv. an acid halide\nStarting from acetic acid, how will you prepare each of the following?\nii. acetic anhydride\niii. acetamide\niv. ethyl acetate\nv. ethyl alcohol\n4.\nWrite an equation for:\n5.\ni. Hydrolysis of acetyl chloride\nWe inc\nii. Reaction of benzoyl chloride with methanol.\niii. Esterification of butan-1-ol with acetic anhydride.\niv. Ammonolysis of butanoyl chloride.\nv. Fischer esterfication of pentanoic acid with ethanol.\n(a) Describe three methods for preparation of carboxylic acids.\n(b) Write the systematic names for the following organic compounds;\nCH\ni.\n0CH, ။\nHO-C-CH-CH-C-OH\niii.\n11.\nCH,\nH,C-CH2-CH-CH2-C-OH\n0\niv.\nO\nH,C-CH2-CH-CH-C-OC2H, H2C=CH-CH-CH-C-NH2\nX\n270\n*\nV.\n-\nHC C-CH-CH-C-OH\nNOT FOR SALE\n(c) Draw the structural formula of the following organic compounds;\ni. 3-ethyl-4-methylpentanoic acid iii. 2-chloropropanoyl bromide\nV.\n3,3-dimethylbutanenitrile\n(d) Complete the following reactions.\ni. CH,CH,CH,COOH + PCI, ii. CH,CH,COOH + SOCI,\niii. CH,CH,CONH2+LIAIH, iv. CH,COOCOCH, + NH,\nv. CH,CH, COOCH, + NaOH\nvi. CHỊCH, COONa + NaOH\nvii. CH,CH2 COOC2H, + LiAlH,\nviii. CH,CH, MgBr + CH,CH,CN\nCaO\nii. ethyl 3-methylbutanoate iv. ethanoic propanoic anhydride",
