      "The monosaccharides are again subdivided on the basis of the type of functional p On the basis of types of functional group monosaccharides may be classified as aldoses or ketoses. There are only two trioses: glyceraldehyde and dihydroxyacetone. Each has two hydroxyl groups, attached to different carbon atoms and one carbonyl group.",
