      "Adenosine Triphosphate",
      "21.1.3 Nutritional Importance Carbohydrates are the most important energy containing nutrients for living organisms. Plant Adenosine triphosphate, also known as contains stored carbohydrates called starch ATP, is a molecule that carries energy while animals contain stored carbohydrates within cells. It is the main energy currency called glycogen. Both, these polymers are of the cell and it is an end product of broken down into the simplest monosaccharide the processes of photophosphorylation units known as glucose, before oxidation. Then (adding a phosphate group to a molecule glucose is oxidized in the body cells by respiration and fermentation. All living using energy from light), cellular different types of pathways (series of things use ATP. It is also used in signal enzymatic chemical reactions) to release convert pathways for cell communication energy. This energy is stored in the form of and is incorporated into deoxyribonucleic molecules known as ATP (adenosine acid (DNA) during DNA synthesis. triphosphate) in the different parts of the body.",
