      "energy.",
      "they have no ester bonds.",
      "They act as structural components of membranes.",
      "They act as protective and insulating coatings.",
      "Nervous tissues are rich in lipids where they play important role in their",
      "functions.",
      "The sub-cutaneous fat serves the role of insulating against atmospheric heat and cold.",
      "Lipids may be saponfiable or non-saponifiable. Fats, oils and waxes are saponifiable while terpenes and steroids are non-saponifiable lipids.",
      "21.4.1",
      "Classification",
      "Lipids have been classified into following three major classes:",
      "1. Simple Lipids",
      "These are the esters of fatty acids with different types of alcohols. These include,",
      "(1). Fats and oils, which yield fatty acids and glycerol upon hydrolysis. (ii). Waxes, which yield fatty acids and long-chain alcohols upon hydrolysis.",
      "(1) Fats and Oils",
      "Both types of compounds are called Triacylglycerols or triglycerides because they are esters composed of three fatty acids joined to glycerol. The difference is on the basis of their physical states at room temperature. Fat is solid at room temperature while oil is liquid at room temperature. These differences in melting points reflect differences in the degree of unsaturation of the constituent fatty acids. Oils contain more un-saturation in the alkyl part of fatty acids than fats. Fatty acids are long chain carboxylic acids contain usually",
      "12-18 carbon atoms per molecule.",
      "291",
      "(ii)",
