      "RNA is formed in the nucleolus and then moves to specialized regions of",
      "while a small amount of DNA also the cytoplasm depending on the type",
      "present in mitochondria.",
      "DNA consists of two strands, arranged in a double helix. These strands are made up of subunits called nucleotides.",
      "DNA is a much longer polymer than RNA. A chromosome, for example, is a single, long DNA",
