        "theory": "Hair dyes are the dyes, used for hair colouring.\nThe adhesive is a substance usually in liquid or semi-liquid states that is used in binding two or more objects together and resists their separation. Adhesives are of two types non-reactive and reactive adhesives. Reactive adhesives are classified into two classes e.g. multi part adhesives and\none part adhesives.\nCC\n331\nNOT FOR SALE\nExercise\nQI. Choose the correct one from the given options.\n1. The monomer pair required for the formation of Nylon 6,6 is\na. hexamethylene diamine + adipic acid.\nb. hexamethylene diamine + sebacoyl chloride.\nc. hexamethylene diamine + decanoic acid.\nd. hexamethylene amine + ethanedioic acid,\n2. Which one is true for DDT?\na. An antibiotic\nc. An antiseptic\n3. The term black gold is used for\na. coal\nc. petroleum\n4. All are petrochemicals except\na. ethylene oxide\nc. cellulose\n5. Multipart adhesive is an example of\na. reactive adhesives.\nc. hot adhesives.\n6. Nail polish removers are mainly composed of\na. propyne\nc. propanal\n7. In the process of cracking\na. small molecule unite together.\nb. large molecules unite together.\nc. large molecules are broken down.\nd. small and large molecules unite together.\n8. Rexine is the manipulated form of\na. plastic (PVC)\nc. lipstick\nb. Non pollutant\nd. Non-degradable\nb. carbon black\nd.\ncoal tar\nb. polypropylene\nd. cyclohexane\nb. contact adhesives.\nd. pressure sensitive adhesives.\nb. propanone\nd. propene\nawaz e\nb. nylon\nd. nail polish\n9. Identify the petrochemical which is not obtained from benzene\na. alkyl benzenes\nc. nitrobenzene\nb. cyclohexane\n332\nd. vinyl chloride\n10. Which of the following is condensation polymer\na. PVC. c. nylon.\nNOT FOR SALE\nb. polythene.\nd. none of these,\n11. (-NH-(CH2)6-CONHCO(CH2)4CO-), is an example of\na.\naddition polymer.\nb. thermosetting polymer.\nc. condensation copolymer (Nylon-6,6). 12. Which one of the following is synthetic polymer?\na. cellulose\nc. silk\nd. homo-polymer.\nb. starch\nd. polythene\n13. Hair dyes are commonly classified into groups\na. 3\nb. 4\n14. All are synthetic adhesives except\na. casein glues\nc. cyanoacrylates\n15. Acrylate base polymers are\na. drying adhesives.\nb. pressure sensitive adhesives.",
