        "content": "Environmental Chemistry<br>Teaching<br>9<br>Assessment<br>1<br>Weightage %<br>CCC<br>After studying this unit, students will be able to:<br>Recognize various chemical reactions, occurring in the atmosphere. (Understanding) Recognize that the release of CO,, SO, NO,, VOCs are associated with the combustion of hydrocarbon-based fuels. (Applying)<br>Outline problems associated with release of pollutants, including acid rain and the formation by free radical reactions of hazardous inorganic and organic compounds e.g PAN. (Analyzing)<br>Describe causes and impacts of urban smog. (Analyzing)<br>Explain greenhouse effect and global warming as resulting in climate change. (Analyzing) Explain the build-up and recognize the adverse effects of ozone in the troposphere. (Applying)<br>Describe the role of CFCs in destroying ozone in the stratosphere. (Applying)<br>← Describe the role of ozone in the stratosphere in reducing the intensity of harmful UV<br>radiation reaching the Earth. (Understanding)<br>List possible alternatives to the use of CFCs. (Applying)<br>Recognize and describe various water pollutants. (Applying) Explain the various parameters of water analysis. (Applying)<br>335<br>Introduction<br>NOT FOR SAT<br>In this unit, we will turn our attention to environmental issues, associated v Earth&#x27;s atmosphere. Air and water pollutions are the major problems in most of World&#x27;s cities. The atmosphere, a part of the environment, acts as repository emissions from combustion and from many other human activities. The air can cleansed by natural mechanisms but these can be overwhelmed by the amount pollutants being produced. Human activities are increasing the atmosphe concentration of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases. In addition, stratospheric ozone shield, which protects us from the ultraviolet rays, is threatened the emission of ozone-destroying chemicals.<br>Likewise, water quality is an important issue. Although most of the water supply returned to the stream flow after use, its quality is necessarily degraded. The quality surface and ground water is of concern due to two distinct points of view, that is, hum health and welfare and the health of aquatic ecosystems.<br>Atmosphere is the envelop of gases,<br>surrounding the Earth&#x27;s surface. It plays<br>Exosphere<br>a key role to sustain life on Earth and<br>save it from the hazardous environment<br>Mesosphere<br>of the outer space. The atmosphere Thermosphere absorbs most of the cosmic rays from the outer space and harmful radiation such as U.V. through ozone (Os) layer. In addition, the atmosphere maintains the heat balance of the earth through absorption of energy from the sun and re-emitted.<br>The atmosphere can be divided into different layers based on their temperature and characteristics. Starting from the surface of the Earth, going vertically upwards, these layers or regions are as follows:<br>i. Troposphere iv. Thermosphere<br>Stratosphere Troposph<br>ii. Stratosphere v. Exosphere<br>336<br>10,000 km<br>500 km<br>85 km<br>50 km<br>14 km<br>Fig: 23.1: Layers of atmosphere.<br>iii. Mesosphere<br>Zone/Sphere<br>Table: 23.1 The Regions of Atmosphere<br>Altitude<br>Temperature<br>S. No.<br>(in km)<br>h<br>range (C)<br>Troposphere<br>0-14<br>1.<br>15 to-56<br>r<br>Stratosphere<br>10-50<br>NgO,, CO, H, O, Ar<br>NOT FOR SALE<br>Important Chemical Species<br>2.<br>-56 to-2<br>O, (ozone), N, O,<br>of<br>3.<br>Mesosphere<br>50-85<br>-2 to-92<br>NO*,0%<br>CL<br>4.<br>Thermosphere<br>85-500<br>-92 to 1200<br>O,NO,0,0,<br>5.<br>Exosphere<br>500-10,000 Above 1500<br>H, He, N2, O2, CO2<br>f<br>1<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Environmental Chemistry\" style=\"width:min(100%,460px);height:auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbeafe;border-radius:10px;margin:12px 0\"><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"90\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"90\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#059669\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"90\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#fee2e2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M178 90H200M258 90H280\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"145\" font-size=\"14\">air</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"145\" font-size=\"14\">water</text><text x=\"287\" y=\"145\" font-size=\"14\">soil</text><text x=\"163\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"14\">environmental pathways</text></svg>",
