      "NOT FOR SAT",
      "In this unit, we will turn our attention to environmental issues, associated v Earth's atmosphere. Air and water pollutions are the major problems in most of World's cities. The atmosphere, a part of the environment, acts as repository emissions from combustion and from many other human activities. The air can cleansed by natural mechanisms but these can be overwhelmed by the amount pollutants being produced. Human activities are increasing the atmosphe concentration of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases. In addition, stratospheric ozone shield, which protects us from the ultraviolet rays, is threatened the emission of ozone-destroying chemicals.",
      "Likewise, water quality is an important issue. Although most of the water supply returned to the stream flow after use, its quality is necessarily degraded. The quality surface and ground water is of concern due to two distinct points of view, that is, hum health and welfare and the health of aquatic ecosystems.",
