        "theory": "4. b\n5. d\n6. a\n9. a\n10. d\n1. c\n7. d\nilab.com\nUnit-21\n3.\na\n4. c\n5. d\n6. a\n9.\nb\n10. c\n11. b\n12.\na\n15. c\nUnit-22\n1.\na\n2.\nd\n3. c\n4. c\n5. a\n6. b\n7. c\n8. a\n9. d\n10. c\n11. c\n12. d\n13. b\n14. a\n15. b\nUnit-23\n1. d\n2. d\n3. a\n4. a\n5. d\n6. d\n7. d\n8. a\n9. C\n10. a\n11. b\n12. a\n13. d\n14. a\n15. d\nUnit-24\n1. b\n2. C\n3. a\n4. a\n5. b\n6. a\n7. d\n8. c\n9. a\n10. d\n11. a\n12. d\n13. b\n14. b\n15. d\n385\nK\nNOT FOR SALE\nGLOSSARY\nAlcohols:- Alcohols are organic compounds, in which a hydroxyl group(-OH) is attached to carbon atom of an alkyl group.\nAlkanes:- These are saturated acyclic hydrocarbons which contain all carbon-carbon single bond.\nAlkyl halide:-The organic compounds in which one or more halogen atoms are directly bonded to carbon atom of an alkyl group.\nAlkylation of Ammonia :- The reaction in which hydrogen atoms of NH3 are replaced\nby alkyl groups.",
        "content": "4. b<br>5. d<br>6. a<br>9. a<br>10. d<br>1. c<br>7. d<br>ilab.com<br>Unit-21<br>3.<br>a<br>4. c<br>5. d<br>6. a<br>9.<br>b<br>10. c<br>11. b<br>12.<br>a<br>15. c<br>Unit-22<br>1.<br>a<br>2.<br>d<br>3. c<br>4. c<br>5. a<br>6. b<br>7. c<br>8. a<br>9. d<br>10. c<br>11. c<br>12. d<br>13. b<br>14. a<br>15. b<br>Unit-23<br>1. d<br>2. d<br>3. a<br>4. a<br>5. d<br>6. d<br>7. d<br>8. a<br>9. C<br>10. a<br>11. b<br>12. a<br>13. d<br>14. a<br>15. d<br>Unit-24<br>1. b<br>2. C<br>3. a<br>4. a<br>5. b<br>6. a<br>7. d<br>8. c<br>9. a<br>10. d<br>11. a<br>12. d<br>13. b<br>14. b<br>15. d<br>385<br>K<br>NOT FOR SALE<br>GLOSSARY<br>Alcohols:- Alcohols are organic compounds, in which a hydroxyl group(-OH) is attached to carbon atom of an alkyl group.<br>Alkanes:- These are saturated acyclic hydrocarbons which contain all carbon-carbon single bond.<br>Alkyl halide:-The organic compounds in which one or more halogen atoms are directly bonded to carbon atom of an alkyl group.<br>Alkylation of Ammonia :- The reaction in which hydrogen atoms of NH3 are replaced<br>by alkyl groups.",
