      "furnace and trapped in a pair of absorbers. Water is absorbed in a sample of magnesium perchlorate (Mg(CIO), of known mass, and carbon dioxide is absorbed by aqueous solution of sodium or potassium hydroxide. The increase in masses of both absorbers is the masses of water and carbon dioxide produced respectively, during combustion.",
