          "text": "The Group – IVA of the periodic table is often referred to as the carbon group. This group consists of five elements carbon (C), silicon (Si), germanium (Ge), tin (Sn) and lead (Pb). This group is present in the middle of periodic table forming a link between more electropositive elements of Group – IA to IIIA and more electronegative elements of Group VA to VIIA. Each element in this group contains four valence electrons. The elements of group – IV A evidentially exhibit an intermediate character. The general electronic configuration of Group – IVA elements in valence shell is ns², np², where n varies from 2 (for carbon) to 6 (for lead), for example, the electronic configuration of carbon is 1s²,2s², 2p².",
